== Problem description ==
<!-- 
Provide a concise description of the issue here. Be  as specific as possible to help readers quickly determine whether or not this is the exact problem they are facing.
 -->

Galaxy A33 screen does not respond at all. Displays no image, but there is a touch input on the entire panel. Replacing the screen does not fix the issue.

== Symptoms ==
<!--
Detail all measurable or observable symptoms in this section. 
-->
* No display(graphics) on screen
* Phone boots normally
* Touchscreen works
* Charges normally

== Solution ==
<!-- 
If the issue has a single, specific solution, provide it in this section and delete the sub-headers below. Otherwise, if there are multiple potential causes for the problem, outline the process of identifying the root cause and offer corresponding solutions below.

-->

The problem is due to a missing VDD_LCD_ELAVDD_7P6 signal. 

=== Repair Steps ===
[[File:DIODE VALUE main fpc galaxy a33 5g.png|center|thumb|Diode Value]]

* Check GR on the connector (you will get a missing GR on a following pin)[[File:BURNED PIN galaxy a33 5g.png|center|thumb|BURNED PIN]]
* Check GR on the Capacitor where the area is burned, if GR is ok then proceed to do the jumper like in the following picture[[File:JUMPER samsung galaxy a33 5g.png|center|thumb|JUMPER]]
* Test the display if it works
* If everything seems fine cover the jumper with UV oil.